<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Polaron · independent phase boundaries</title>
<style>
:root{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:#183345;background:#edf2f4}body{margin:0}header{background:#123647;color:white;padding:24px 4vw}h1{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:29px}p{line-height:1.5}header p{max-width:1100px;margin:8px 0}.wrap{padding:20px 4vw}.bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:12px 0}button,select,input,textarea{font:inherit;border:1px solid #9fb5bf;border-radius:6px;padding:8px;background:white;color:#183345}button{cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.4}.layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(280px,1fr);gap:20px}.panel{background:white;border-radius:12px;padding:18px}.imagebox{overflow:auto;background:#27313a;max-height:75vh}canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;cursor:crosshair;touch-action:none}label{display:block;margin:12px 0}textarea{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;min-height:100px}.hint{font-size:14px;color:#496371}.chip{background:#dcebf0;border-radius:18px;padding:6px 10px}#error{color:#a12828;white-space:pre-wrap;margin:10px 0}.legend{font-size:13px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}.legend span{border-left:10px solid;padding-left:5px}fieldset{border:1px solid #bbcdd5;border-radius:7px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}@media(max-width:1000px){.layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}}input[type=checkbox]{accent-color:#096980}
</style>
<header><h1>Independent phase-boundary review</h1><p id="purpose"></p><p>Inspect the raw BSE crop and draw the visible phase boundaries. These pages omit batch labels, quality flags and algorithm predictions. Bright appearance is not a chemical label. Leave ambiguous regions uncertain; an unmeasurable image is a useful result.</p></header>
<main class="wrap"><div class="bar"><label>Crop <select id="roi"></select></label><button id="prev">Previous</button><button id="next">Next</button><span class="chip" id="progress"></span><button id="export">Download review JSON</button><label>Resume saved review <input id="import" type="file" accept=".json"></label></div><div id="error" role="alert"></div>
<div class="layout"><section class="panel"><h2 id="cropname">Raw image</h2><div class="bar"><select id="phase"><option value="0">Void · cyan</option><option value="2">Bright appearance · gold</option><option value="1">Residual solid · green</option><option value="255">Uncertain / ignore · magenta</option></select><button id="finish">Finish polygon</button><button id="cancel">Cancel points</button><button id="undo">Undo polygon</button></div>
<div class="bar"><label><input id="show" type="checkbox" checked> Show my annotations</label><button id="fit">Fit width</button><button id="actual">One image pixel per display pixel</button></div>
<div class="imagebox"><canvas id="canvas"></canvas></div><p class="hint">Click polygon corners, then finish. Later polygons overwrite earlier ones. Use residual-solid polygons beside phase boundaries as well as interiors; labelling only obvious interiors cannot test boundary errors.</p>
<div class="legend"><span style="border-color:#23b9d7">Void</span><span style="border-color:#f5af1e">Bright</span><span style="border-color:#4caf77">Solid</span><span style="border-color:#d552bf">Ignore</span></div>
<label><input id="background" type="checkbox"> I inspected the whole crop: all unpainted pixels are residual solid.</label><p class="hint">Leave this off for partial labels. Unpainted and uncertain pixels are excluded from comparison. Whole-crop masks are needed for object-size and width errors; cropped objects have additional exclusions.</p></section>
<aside class="panel"><h2>Review record</h2><fieldset><legend>Complete after inspection</legend><label>Reviewer <input id="reviewer" placeholder="Your name"></label><label>Can the phases be measured in the labelled regions? <select id="measurable"><option value="">Choose after inspection</option><option value="true">Yes, within labelled regions</option><option value="false">No, image quality prevents measurement</option></select></label><label>Have you previously seen batch labels or algorithm overlays for this image? <select id="exposure"><option value="not_answered">Choose</option><option value="none">No previous exposure</option><option value="prior_exposure">Yes, or I am unsure</option></select></label><label><input id="independent" type="checkbox"> I drew these boundaries from the raw image without copying an algorithm mask.</label><label>Notes <textarea id="notes" placeholder="Which boundaries are ambiguous? Are bright rims part of an object? Describe pore vs residual-solid uncertainty."></textarea></label><label><input id="reviewed" type="checkbox"> Mark this crop reviewed</label></fieldset>
<p class="hint">Your drawing independence is a reviewer declaration. Previous exposure remains recorded; hiding hints now cannot erase it. Reviews do not automatically change a model or establish phase chemistry.</p><p class="hint">The browser saves progress locally. Download JSON for a durable handoff. Each review packet has separate storage and export identity.</p><details><summary>Evaluation scope</summary><p class="hint">Pixel comparisons use only labelled regions. Partial masks cannot support object-size/width accuracy. ROI results are not full-site KPI accuracy. These are selected examples from previously explored data; crops and pixels are not additional independent material samples.</p><p class="hint">Development and held-out-site pages stay separate. The coordinator must fix method choices before releasing held-out results. This is procedural separation on a shared disk, not access control.</p></details></aside></div></main>
<script id="review-data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script>
<script>
'use strict';
const data=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('review-data').textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id),rois=data.rois;
const key='polaron-independent-'+data.packet_id;
const blank=()=>({schema_version:1,packet_id:data.packet_id,rois:rois.map(r=>({id:r.id,review_status:'unreviewed',measurable:null,reviewer:'',notes:'',background:'unlabelled',polygons:[],independent_drawing:false,prior_exposure:'not_answered'}))});
let state=blank(),index=0,points=[],bitmap=null,loadToken=0;
const colors={0:'#23b9d7',1:'#4caf77',2:'#f5af1e',255:'#d552bf'};
function validate(s){
 if(s.schema_version!==1||s.packet_id!==data.packet_id||!Array.isArray(s.rois)||s.rois.length!==rois.length||new Set(s.rois.map(a=>a.id)).size!==rois.length)throw Error('Wrong packet or missing/duplicate crop IDs.');
 for(const a of s.rois){const r=rois.find(r=>r.id===a.id);if(!r)throw Error('Unknown crop ID.');
  if(!['unreviewed','reviewed'].includes(a.review_status)||![null,true,false].includes(a.measurable)||typeof a.independent_drawing!=='boolean'||!['not_answered','none','prior_exposure'].includes(a.prior_exposure)||typeof a.reviewer!=='string'||typeof a.notes!=='string'||!['solid','unlabelled'].includes(a.background))throw Error('Invalid review record.');
  if(!Array.isArray(a.polygons)||a.polygons.some(p=>![0,1,2,255].includes(p.class_id)||!Array.isArray(p.points)||p.points.length<3||p.points.some(q=>!Array.isArray(q)||q.length!==2||!q.every(Number.isFinite)||q[0]<0||q[0]>=r.W||q[1]<0||q[1]>=r.H)))throw Error('Invalid polygon coordinates or class.');
  if(a.review_status==='reviewed'&&(!a.reviewer.trim()||a.measurable===null||!a.independent_drawing||a.prior_exposure==='not_answered'||(a.measurable&&a.background!=='solid'&&!a.polygons.some(p=>p.class_id!==255))))throw Error('Reviewed crop needs reviewer, measurability, exposure, independent drawing and labelled regions.');
 }return s;
}
try{const saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key));if(saved)state=validate(saved)}catch(e){$('error').textContent='Saved state was unavailable or invalid. Import a downloaded review to resume.'}
function ann(){return state.rois.find(a=>a.id===rois[index].id)}
function progress(){$('progress').textContent=state.rois.filter(a=>a.review_status==='reviewed').length+' / '+rois.length+' reviewed'}
function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(key,JSON.stringify(state))}catch(e){$('error').textContent='Local storage failed; download JSON before closing.'}progress()}
function invalidate(){ann().review_status='unreviewed';$('reviewed').checked=false}
function draw(){const c=$('canvas'),ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.clearRect(0,0,c.width,c.height);if(bitmap)ctx.drawImage(bitmap,0,0);if($('show').checked)for(const p of ann().polygons){ctx.beginPath();p.points.forEach(([x,y],i)=>i?ctx.lineTo(x,y):ctx.moveTo(x,y));ctx.closePath();ctx.fillStyle=colors[p.class_id]+'55';ctx.fill();ctx.strokeStyle=colors[p.class_id];ctx.lineWidth=1.5;ctx.stroke()}if(points.length){ctx.beginPath();points.forEach(([x,y],i)=>i?ctx.lineTo(x,y):ctx.moveTo(x,y));ctx.strokeStyle=colors[$('phase').value];ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.stroke();for(const [x,y] of points)ctx.fillRect(x-2,y-2,4,4)}}
function load(){points=[];bitmap=null;const token=++loadToken,r=rois[index],a=ann();$('roi').value=String(index);$('cropname').textContent='Raw image · '+r.id+' · '+r.W+' × '+r.H+' px';$('canvas').width=r.W;$('canvas').height=r.H;draw();const image=new Image();image.onload=()=>{if(token!==loadToken)return;bitmap=image;draw()};image.src=r.image;$('background').checked=a.background==='solid';$('reviewer').value=a.reviewer;$('notes').value=a.notes;$('measurable').value=a.measurable===null?'':String(a.measurable);$('exposure').value=a.prior_exposure;$('independent').checked=a.independent_drawing;$('reviewed').checked=a.review_status==='reviewed';$('prev').disabled=index===0;$('next').disabled=index===rois.length-1;progress()}
rois.forEach((r,i)=>{const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=i;o.textContent=r.id;$('roi').append(o)});
$('purpose').textContent=data.kind==='held_out_site'?'Held-out measurement packet. Keep annotations/results separate until development method choices are fixed.':data.kind==='feedback_development'?'First-drop development packet. Organiser feedback is already known; this is failure analysis, not unseen validation.':'Development measurement packet. Review before evaluating methods or selecting changes.';
$('roi').onchange=()=>{index=Number($('roi').value);load()};$('prev').onclick=()=>{index--;load()};$('next').onclick=()=>{index++;load()};
$('canvas').onclick=e=>{const r=rois[index],rect=e.target.getBoundingClientRect();points.push([Math.min(r.W-1,Math.max(0,(e.clientX-rect.left)*r.W/rect.width)),Math.min(r.H-1,Math.max(0,(e.clientY-rect.top)*r.H/rect.height))]);draw()};
$('finish').onclick=()=>{if(points.length<3){$('error').textContent='A polygon needs at least three corners.';return}ann().polygons.push({class_id:Number($('phase').value),points:points.map(p=>p.map(Math.round))});points=[];invalidate();$('error').textContent='';save();draw()};
$('cancel').onclick=()=>{points=[];draw()};$('undo').onclick=()=>{ann().polygons.pop();invalidate();save();draw()};$('show').onchange=draw;
$('fit').onclick=()=>{$('canvas').style.width='100%'};$('actual').onclick=()=>{$('canvas').style.width=rois[index].W+'px'};
for(const id of ['reviewer','notes'])$(id).oninput=()=>{ann()[id]=$(id).value;invalidate();save()};
$('background').onchange=()=>{ann().background=$('background').checked?'solid':'unlabelled';invalidate();save();draw()};
$('measurable').onchange=()=>{ann().measurable=$('measurable').value===''?null:$('measurable').value==='true';invalidate();save()};
$('exposure').onchange=()=>{ann().prior_exposure=$('exposure').value;invalidate();save()};$('independent').onchange=()=>{ann().independent_drawing=$('independent').checked;invalidate();save()};
$('reviewed').onchange=()=>{ann().review_status=$('reviewed').checked?'reviewed':'unreviewed';try{validate(state);$('error').textContent='';save()}catch(e){invalidate();$('error').textContent=e.message}};
$('export').onclick=()=>{try{if(points.length)throw Error('Finish or cancel the current polygon before downloading.');validate(state);const url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(state,null,2)],{type:'application/json'}));const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='polaron_'+data.kind+'_boundaries.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);$('error').textContent=''}catch(e){$('error').textContent=e.message}};
$('import').onchange=async()=>{try{const incoming=validate(JSON.parse(await $('import').files[0].text()));state=incoming;save();load();$('error').textContent=''}catch(e){$('error').textContent=e.message}};
load();
</script></html>
